cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Gauntlet: merge-blocking evaluation gates for generative AI features"
message: "If you refer to this harness or to an evidence pack it produced, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kelly-Reif
    given-names: Chelsea
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChelseaKR/gauntlet"
url: "https://chelseakr.github.io/gauntlet/"
abstract: >-
  YAML-driven evaluation gates that run against a deployed generative-AI feature over HTTP or a
  Python callable, fail the build when a gate fails, and emit the run as a diffable JSON pack and
  a reviewer-readable evidence document cross-referenced to California's published GenAI risk and
  procurement framework. It evaluates a feature in its context rather than a foundation model, and
  depends on no model vendor. Aligned to that framework, not approved, endorsed, or certified by
  the State of California or any of its departments.
keywords:
  - evaluation
  - generative AI
  - continuous integration
  - prompt injection
  - public-interest technology
  - procurement
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-15"
